1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,041
PROVINCIAL CITY OF MILS

2
00:00:09,125 --> 00:00:11,083
I don't see any weapons on you.

3
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:12,083
You a mercenary?

4
00:00:12,083 --> 00:00:15,166
Came to make it big by answering the
call to conquer the ruins, huh?

5
00:00:15,166 --> 00:00:19,125
Yes, though I've never been
to such a flourishing town before.

6
00:00:19,166 --> 00:00:21,041
Milza was a good hike for me.

7
00:00:21,041 --> 00:00:23,125
It's not Milza. It's Mils.

8
00:00:23,125 --> 00:00:26,166
Good grief, this is the problem
with country bumpkins.

9
00:00:26,208 --> 00:00:28,125
Hey, we can let him pass, yeah?

10
00:00:29,166 --> 00:00:36,041
The marquis wants us to let in as many
mercenaries headed for the ruins as possible.

11
00:00:36,041 --> 00:00:38,083
You're good, so move it along.

12
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:41,000
Thank you very much. I'll do my best.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,083
No patdowns or luggage checks.

14
00:00:45,125 --> 00:00:47,083
They're surprisingly lax.

15
00:00:50,041 --> 00:00:51,125
Things are going smoothly.

16
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:55,208
A private room?

17
00:00:56,125 --> 00:00:59,208
We do have them,
but they're 2,000 maca a night.

18
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:02,000
He's not looking upon me favorably.

19
00:01:02,041 --> 00:01:03,125
Oh, maybe it's because...

20
00:01:03,166 --> 00:01:07,166
I had a long journey, so my clothes
have gotten rather dirty.

21
00:01:07,208 --> 00:01:11,000
I'd appreciate it if you have anything
to wear and know where I could wash up.

22
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:12,041
Yes, yes!

23
00:01:12,083 --> 00:01:13,125
Understood!

24
00:01:13,166 --> 00:01:15,083
Let me show you right away!

25
00:01:15,083 --> 00:01:16,125
Talk about turning on a dime.

26
00:01:16,166 --> 00:01:19,041
By the way, may I ask your name?

27
00:01:19,208 --> 00:01:21,125
It's Hati Skoll.

28
00:02:52,166 --> 00:02:57,125
THE WOMAN KNOWN AS THE PRINCESS KNIGHT

29
00:03:01,041 --> 00:03:03,125
I don't see anyone acting
suspicious of outsiders.

30
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,208
Seems like a fairly safe city, too.

31
00:03:07,125 --> 00:03:12,208
It has all the typical shops you'd
expect from a Western fantasy town.

32
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,166
I wonder if any of them sell magic items.

33
00:03:15,208 --> 00:03:18,125
Is this... one of those adventurer's guilds?

34
00:03:20,208 --> 00:03:23,041
That'll do for getting a lay of the land.

35
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:29,208
That's good.

36
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,208
The flavor is pretty rustic,

37
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,125
but I shouldn't underestimate
the food in this world.

38
00:03:36,166 --> 00:03:38,125
Taverns are great.

39
00:03:38,125 --> 00:03:40,166
Spirits run high and voices run loud.

40
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,041
Makes it easy to eavesdrop.

41
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:45,125
Perfect for gathering information.

42
00:03:45,166 --> 00:03:49,083
The continent's loaded with monstrous
knights and armies in every nation,

43
00:03:49,125 --> 00:03:51,041
so who d'ya think is the strongest?

44
00:03:51,083 --> 00:03:55,083
How about the Brilliant Brigade led by the
beautiful Mad Emperor Falkendotzine?

45
00:03:55,083 --> 00:03:58,000
They're famously undefeated.

46
00:03:58,125 --> 00:04:00,000
But the Magnar Kingdom to the north

47
00:04:00,041 --> 00:04:02,000
has the Order of the White Wolves, right?

48
00:04:02,083 --> 00:04:05,125
There's also the Holy Order of the Purge
in Yonato Duchy to the west.

49
00:04:05,208 --> 00:04:09,083
And our very own kingdom of Ulza
has the Order of Monster Slayers.

50
00:04:09,125 --> 00:04:10,166
Still...

51
00:04:10,208 --> 00:04:14,166
Yeah, the strongest in the continent
has to be the Black Dragon Knights

52
00:04:14,208 --> 00:04:17,208
of the Bakoss Empire, who wiped
out the Holy Empire of Neah.

53
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:21,041
I hear their Five Dragoons alone
rival an entire army.

54
00:04:21,125 --> 00:04:24,125
They've got Humanity's Strongest
and the Hero Slayer, y'know?

55
00:04:24,125 --> 00:04:27,208
What man wouldn't get invested in them?

56
00:04:37,083 --> 00:04:39,125
I guess we should decide our future plans.

57
00:04:39,208 --> 00:04:43,166
Our top priority is connecting with someone
who can read the scroll of forbidden magic.

58
00:04:43,166 --> 00:04:45,166
That means finding the Witch of Taboos

59
00:04:45,208 --> 00:04:47,208
hiding in the Land of Golden-Eyed Monsters.

60
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,000
There's also...

61
00:04:50,083 --> 00:04:52,000
the monster enhancement solution.

62
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:54,000
A way to improve Piggymaru's abilities.

63
00:04:56,125 --> 00:04:57,125
Hold on...

64
00:04:57,125 --> 00:05:02,125
Mils has been bustling since the marquis
called for conquest of the ruins.

65
00:05:02,125 --> 00:05:06,041
Discovering a new floor always
breathes life into this place!

66
00:05:09,041 --> 00:05:13,041
"How to create an enhancement solution using
powdered bone from a skeleton king."

67
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,125
And the skeleton king's habitat...

68
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,041
is the Mils Ruins!

69
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,208
They want those dungeon ruins cleared, huh?

70
00:05:22,041 --> 00:05:25,125
Everyone, thank you all for gathering here!

71
00:05:25,125 --> 00:05:27,041
I am Cred Hurkley.

72
00:05:27,166 --> 00:05:30,166
You may know me as
Marquis Hurkley the connoisseur.

73
00:05:31,041 --> 00:05:35,125
We've recently uncovered a new floor
here in the Mils Ruins.

74
00:05:35,125 --> 00:05:38,083
Now I'd like to task you with exploring it.

75
00:05:38,166 --> 00:05:43,041
Whosoever obtains the Dragon Eye
Chalice sleeping within the ruins

76
00:05:43,083 --> 00:05:45,125
shall be awarded 300 gold pieces!

77
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Whoa!

78
00:05:47,041 --> 00:05:51,125
I'll also pay good money
for any other treasure you bring back.

79
00:05:51,125 --> 00:05:54,125
You're free to use any monster
materials you obtain as you wish!

80
00:05:54,166 --> 00:05:58,041
Good. Sounds like I can keep bone powder
from the skeleton king.

81
00:05:58,166 --> 00:06:00,166
We'll now begin the registration process.

82
00:06:00,166 --> 00:06:02,125
Those participating, line up over here!

83
00:06:04,208 --> 00:06:07,208
You can hide your face, but I can still tell!

84
00:06:07,208 --> 00:06:10,083
You're incredibly beautiful.

85
00:06:10,125 --> 00:06:13,000
Plus, you're brimming with grace.

86
00:06:13,041 --> 00:06:16,125
Surely you must be someone of renown, hmm?

87
00:06:17,041 --> 00:06:18,041
Excuse me?

88
00:06:19,041 --> 00:06:22,083
Even your voice is superb, isn't it?

89
00:06:22,083 --> 00:06:23,166
It's almost like...

90
00:06:23,166 --> 00:06:26,208
you're the paladin captain
of a certain nation!

91
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,083
Seras Ashrain from the Holy Empire of Neah?

92
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:31,166
That former knight captain
with a bounty on her head?

93
00:06:31,208 --> 00:06:33,083
She's an elven knight captain, right?

94
00:06:33,083 --> 00:06:34,208
A former knight captain?

95
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:39,125
To tell the truth, I've met her once before.

96
00:06:39,125 --> 00:06:42,125
She was quite, quite the beauty.

97
00:06:42,125 --> 00:06:45,166
But even though I invited her to dinner,

98
00:06:45,208 --> 00:06:48,208
she treated me with great disdain!

99
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:51,083
I don't recall ever meeting you.

100
00:06:52,083 --> 00:06:55,125
You took that high-and-mighty
attitude with me back then too,

101
00:06:55,166 --> 00:06:58,083
brushing me off
with utter disinterest, didn't you?

102
00:06:58,083 --> 00:06:59,125
However...

103
00:06:59,166 --> 00:07:03,125
Thanks to that, your face has
been burned into my memory!

104
00:07:03,125 --> 00:07:07,083
Along with those lewd, outrageous,
and full, ripe breasts!

105
00:07:07,083 --> 00:07:09,166
Excuse me, but I think you
have the wrong person.

106
00:07:09,166 --> 00:07:13,083
In that case, what about your ears?

107
00:07:13,083 --> 00:07:16,208
Unlike humans,
elves all have sharply pointed ears!

108
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:21,125
However, there are very few elves
in this area around the kingdom of Ulza.

109
00:07:21,125 --> 00:07:23,125
But, but, but...

110
00:07:23,125 --> 00:07:26,083
As you all well know,
the former captain from a certain country

111
00:07:26,083 --> 00:07:29,166
who's been on the run lately is
a high elf known as the Princess Knight!

112
00:07:30,208 --> 00:07:33,083
You might fool idiots, but you can't fool me!

113
00:07:33,125 --> 00:07:38,083
Those pointy ears are proof
that you're Seras Ashrain!

114
00:07:38,125 --> 00:07:40,208
How do you like that?!

115
00:07:40,208 --> 00:07:43,208
The one who revealed the Princess
Knight's true identity was me!

116
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,208
The Flash, Monk Droghetti!

117
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Huh?

118
00:07:49,208 --> 00:07:50,166
What...?

119
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,083
It's that woman from the forest.

120
00:07:52,125 --> 00:07:54,000
I-Impossible!

121
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,041
A-And your face! Your face is different too!

122
00:07:56,041 --> 00:07:58,125
My name is Mist Balukas.

123
00:07:58,125 --> 00:08:00,166
I'm not Seras Ashrain.

124
00:08:00,208 --> 00:08:02,125
Are you satisfied now?

125
00:08:02,166 --> 00:08:04,166
N-No way! This can't be!

126
00:08:04,208 --> 00:08:06,208
He had the wrong person
after all that fuss?

127
00:08:06,208 --> 00:08:09,125
I seriously thought it was the
knight captain for a moment.

128
00:08:09,208 --> 00:08:11,041
You won't get away with this!

129
00:08:11,083 --> 00:08:15,000
Every last one of you beautiful women is...

130
00:08:15,041 --> 00:08:18,125
I won't forget this, Mist Balukas!

131
00:08:19,041 --> 00:08:21,083
Talk about unfounded resentment.

132
00:08:24,125 --> 00:08:26,208
I'll need to do some
shopping before I delve.

133
00:08:37,041 --> 00:08:38,041
Excuse me.

134
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,041
Are you here to answer
the marquis's call as well?

135
00:08:42,041 --> 00:08:43,041
Kind of.

136
00:08:43,041 --> 00:08:45,041
Tough break back there, huh?

137
00:08:45,125 --> 00:08:48,000
It wasn't much of a problem.

138
00:08:48,041 --> 00:08:51,041
Even so, you should probably be careful.

139
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:56,125
That man who harassed you was
bright red with rage and hatred.

140
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,125
Every now and then,
I wind up crossing people like that.

141
00:09:00,166 --> 00:09:03,000
It's easier once they hate me and stay away

142
00:09:03,041 --> 00:09:06,000
rather than try to get close
for my affections.

143
00:09:06,041 --> 00:09:09,125
I can tell you're intentionally
trying to avoid interacting with others.

144
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,125
That said, I still have a request.

145
00:09:13,166 --> 00:09:16,166
You want advice so you aren't swindled

146
00:09:16,166 --> 00:09:19,041
when buying items to explore the ruins?

147
00:09:19,083 --> 00:09:20,208
I'll pay you for your assistance.

148
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:26,125
Well, you see... Truth be told,
I am in need of travel funds.

149
00:09:26,125 --> 00:09:29,166
So that's a beneficial proposal
for me as well.

150
00:09:29,166 --> 00:09:31,166
Then we have an agreement?

151
00:09:32,208 --> 00:09:34,125
I'm Mist Balukas.

152
00:09:34,208 --> 00:09:36,000
Hati Skoll.

153
00:09:37,125 --> 00:09:38,125
I see.

154
00:09:38,125 --> 00:09:40,125
This woman is keen to lies.

155
00:09:40,125 --> 00:09:42,125
An alias, obviously.

156
00:09:43,125 --> 00:09:45,208
You and I both have our secrets,

157
00:09:45,208 --> 00:09:48,125
so there's no point in sharing
our real names for now.

158
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:49,208
Agreed.

159
00:09:56,125 --> 00:09:57,208
You've been a big help.

160
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,208
Here's the fee I promised.

161
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,041
This much?

162
00:10:01,083 --> 00:10:04,083
By my math, you saved
me over three silver pieces.

163
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:07,166
Then I will gratefully take these silvers.

164
00:10:07,208 --> 00:10:12,208
Though this is much more than I expected,
so I'm honestly hesitant to accept it.

165
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,208
Thank you very much.

166
00:10:14,208 --> 00:10:17,000
Now then, I'll be on my way.

167
00:10:18,083 --> 00:10:19,083
She's so light.

168
00:10:21,083 --> 00:10:22,083
You okay?

169
00:10:23,166 --> 00:10:25,166
You have bags under your eyes.

170
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:29,166
I-Indeed. I haven't slept well
for several days.

171
00:10:29,166 --> 00:10:32,000
I-I'm fine, though.

172
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:33,208
Sorry to worry you.

173
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:42,041
Hmm? What next?

174
00:10:42,208 --> 00:10:46,125
Naturally, we start conquering
the ruins of Mils.

175
00:10:48,041 --> 00:10:50,041
MILS RUINS

176
00:11:05,208 --> 00:11:07,041
It's a little ox demon!

177
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,083
Run!

178
00:11:09,125 --> 00:11:12,166
Like a miniature version of
the minotaurs from the Ruins of Disposal?

179
00:11:12,208 --> 00:11:13,166
Paralyze.

180
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
Poison.

181
00:11:16,041 --> 00:11:17,208
My Paralyze and Poison both worked.

182
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,208
Seems the monsters from the Ruins of Disposal
had exceptionally tough hides after all.

183
00:11:23,041 --> 00:11:24,166
O-Over there!

184
00:11:24,166 --> 00:11:26,208
That's where we saw the
little ox demon! Please!

185
00:11:27,041 --> 00:11:28,208
Sure, leave it to me.

186
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,041
I-It's dead...

187
00:11:31,041 --> 00:11:33,083
Looks like another mercenary defeated it.

188
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,041
Wait, this thing isn't even injured!

189
00:11:36,083 --> 00:11:38,208
No, hold on. If you look closely...

190
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:41,041
This is a dagger wound, right?

191
00:11:41,041 --> 00:11:43,125
Huh?! They killed it in
one blow with a dagger?!

192
00:11:44,125 --> 00:11:47,041
It wasn't a single hit from a dagger, no.

193
00:11:48,083 --> 00:11:52,125
Right now, I'm not feeling any
threat from the monsters here.

194
00:11:53,041 --> 00:11:54,125
Stats: Open.

195
00:11:56,166 --> 00:11:58,208
Not getting much experience either.

196
00:11:59,083 --> 00:12:01,000
Guess I'll move on at a brisk pace.

197
00:12:01,166 --> 00:12:05,083
I know you two are strong,
so I have a request for you.

198
00:12:05,208 --> 00:12:08,000
I want you to make that woman

199
00:12:08,041 --> 00:12:11,083
who humiliated me in the plaza
regret ever being born.

200
00:12:11,083 --> 00:12:13,125
Any specifics? You want her killed?

201
00:12:13,125 --> 00:12:15,000
Yes, kill her!

202
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:16,208
Though if she begs for her life

203
00:12:16,208 --> 00:12:20,041
and you decide she's truly sorry
for what she did to me,

204
00:12:20,041 --> 00:12:22,041
then don't kill her quickly.

205
00:12:22,083 --> 00:12:25,166
You sure are pissed at her, huh?

206
00:12:25,208 --> 00:12:27,041
She seriously ticked me off!

207
00:12:27,041 --> 00:12:29,000
That woman made a fool of me,

208
00:12:29,041 --> 00:12:32,208
and the thought of her still breathing
and going on without a care...

209
00:12:32,208 --> 00:12:37,125
It makes my gut seethe!
Makes me want to claw out my chest!

210
00:12:37,208 --> 00:12:41,166
Until I see that smug face
twisted in despair as she dies,

211
00:12:41,166 --> 00:12:43,125
I'll never sleep in peace!

212
00:12:43,125 --> 00:12:45,125
Once you kill her, I'll feed her to them!

213
00:12:45,166 --> 00:12:49,166
I'll feed that pretty face
and body to the monsters!

214
00:12:49,166 --> 00:12:53,000
W-We don't care if that's how you
want to dispose of her,

215
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,166
but at least let us have our fun first, okay?

216
00:12:56,125 --> 00:13:00,125
I could tell she had an amazing body,
even through her garb.

217
00:13:00,125 --> 00:13:01,166
Of course!

218
00:13:01,166 --> 00:13:03,083
Use her until she's in tatters.

219
00:13:03,083 --> 00:13:04,125
She dismissed me twice.

220
00:13:04,166 --> 00:13:06,000
Me! Of all people!

221
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,041
That woman is monster feed!

222
00:13:07,083 --> 00:13:08,208
Monster feed, monster feed, monster feed!

223
00:13:11,041 --> 00:13:12,041
Who the hell're you?!

224
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,125
You eavesdroppin' on us?

225
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:15,166
You're an irredeemable lot.

226
00:13:15,208 --> 00:13:16,208
What?!

227
00:13:16,208 --> 00:13:20,041
Who do you think you're talking to,
brat?! I'll kill you!

228
00:13:20,041 --> 00:13:21,083
You snap way too much.

229
00:13:22,166 --> 00:13:25,166
Some green brat trying
to act like a damn saint?

230
00:13:25,166 --> 00:13:28,083
Let's just kill him quick. He's in the way!

231
00:13:28,208 --> 00:13:32,000
It's pretty common for folks
to die in ruins, y'know?

232
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:33,000
Hold on a moment.

233
00:13:33,041 --> 00:13:34,208
Huh? What's this?

234
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:38,041
I'm sorry. Please spare me.

235
00:13:38,208 --> 00:13:42,041
Begging for your life the instant you
realize you're outmatched?

236
00:13:42,041 --> 00:13:44,208
Too bad you can't take it back onceâ€”

237
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:45,208
Paralyze.

238
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,125
Wh-What?!

239
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:48,166
I can't move!

240
00:13:48,166 --> 00:13:50,041
How...?

241
00:13:50,041 --> 00:13:52,041
What did you do?!

242
00:13:52,083 --> 00:13:53,041
Who knows?

243
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:55,041
More importantly, who were you gonna kill?

244
00:13:55,125 --> 00:13:56,083
Too bad.

245
00:13:56,125 --> 00:13:59,000
My own villainy makes me want to puke.

246
00:13:59,125 --> 00:14:01,125
Probably because it reminds me of them.

247
00:14:02,208 --> 00:14:03,166
Poison.

248
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:05,000
What?!

249
00:14:07,125 --> 00:14:09,125
Exterminating guys like you

250
00:14:09,125 --> 00:14:11,083
feels strangely satisfying.

251
00:14:11,083 --> 00:14:13,041
It's surprisingly nice.

252
00:14:13,083 --> 00:14:18,083
I won't forget this! I'll make you regret it!

253
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,083
Are you stupid?

254
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:24,125
That's exactly why I'm stomping
you out here and now.

255
00:14:32,125 --> 00:14:35,125
Seems you're the ones becoming monster feed.

256
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,166
I guess I'll hit the new floor
if I go one more down.

257
00:14:42,166 --> 00:14:45,083
I'd like to take a break
before setting foot into it.

258
00:14:46,083 --> 00:14:48,125
It is what it is. I'll backtrack a bit.

259
00:14:55,083 --> 00:14:57,083
About three hours of sleep, huh?

260
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,208
Thanks for keeping a lookout.

261
00:15:09,125 --> 00:15:10,208
What's the matter?

262
00:15:11,041 --> 00:15:13,083
THE SABER TIGERS
- There's something unprecedented
happening in these ruins right now.

263
00:15:13,083 --> 00:15:14,208
There's something unprecedented
happening in these ruins right now.

264
00:15:14,208 --> 00:15:17,041
Monsters are dying
in strange ways in random places.

265
00:15:17,041 --> 00:15:18,166
- They are?
- Yeah.

266
00:15:18,166 --> 00:15:20,208
FOSSE, SABER TIGER VICE CAPTAIN
- The funny thing is we can't
figure out what's killing them.

267
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,125
The funny thing is we can't
figure out what's killing them.

268
00:15:22,166 --> 00:15:25,000
We just know their skin turns deathly pale.

269
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,125
CAPTAIN LILY ADAMANTINE
- Both strong and weak monsters alike
are falling in this strange manner.

270
00:15:27,125 --> 00:15:28,125
Both strong and weak monsters alike
are falling in this strange manner.

271
00:15:28,125 --> 00:15:32,000
Even the monsters on floor 14,
which we were the first to reach.

272
00:15:32,125 --> 00:15:36,166
As the leader of the Saber Tigers,
I value my comrades above all else.

273
00:15:36,208 --> 00:15:39,125
It's regrettable, but we're pulling out now.

274
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,208
Do you want to return
to the surface with us?

275
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,166
No, though I'm grateful for the offer.

276
00:15:44,208 --> 00:15:46,041
I see.

277
00:15:46,083 --> 00:15:51,083
Well, if you see any of the other mercs,
do us a favor and pass along the news.

278
00:15:51,125 --> 00:15:52,208
I will.

279
00:15:56,041 --> 00:15:58,041
Now then, I should get moving.

280
00:15:59,125 --> 00:16:00,125
Yeah, that's right.

281
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:04,125
They probably mean the corpses
of monsters I killed with my skill.

282
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
If word of the unusual situation spreads,
it'll mean fewer mercenaries.

283
00:16:08,125 --> 00:16:11,000
This might be a lucky break for me.

284
00:16:21,166 --> 00:16:25,000
Is that the Dragon Eye Chalice?

285
00:16:27,041 --> 00:16:31,125
I'll bet this thing moves.

286
00:16:32,083 --> 00:16:37,166
Anyone familiar with fiction
from modern Japan could anticipate that.

287
00:16:38,041 --> 00:16:39,041
Paralyze.

288
00:16:41,208 --> 00:16:42,208
Poison.

289
00:16:47,041 --> 00:16:49,125
Piggymaru, can I ask you to keep watch?

290
00:16:51,208 --> 00:16:55,125
So, this thing is the prized item
of this event?

291
00:16:56,166 --> 00:16:57,166
Sure is pretty.

292
00:17:02,041 --> 00:17:04,083
Now, what should we do?

293
00:17:07,208 --> 00:17:08,166
It's you?

294
00:17:08,166 --> 00:17:10,166
WANDERING WARRIOR MIST BALUKAS
- I thought I would be the first one here
with the other mercenaries pulling out.

295
00:17:10,208 --> 00:17:13,041
I thought I would be the first one here
with the other mercenaries pulling out.

296
00:17:13,125 --> 00:17:16,000
I guess I lost my chance taking a rest

297
00:17:16,041 --> 00:17:18,041
after some trouble with a pack of monsters.

298
00:17:18,166 --> 00:17:20,166
If you need this, I'll let you have it.

299
00:17:20,166 --> 00:17:22,208
Huh? What did you just say?

300
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,125
If you want it, it's yours.

301
00:17:25,083 --> 00:17:27,041
Wh-What do you want in return?

302
00:17:27,041 --> 00:17:29,041
Three hundred gold is...

303
00:17:29,041 --> 00:17:31,041
There's nothing I really want.

304
00:17:31,041 --> 00:17:33,125
I-I cannot besmirch my honor like that.

305
00:17:33,166 --> 00:17:35,166
You're in a hurry, right?

306
00:17:35,208 --> 00:17:38,166
Though you should be getting proper sleep.

307
00:17:38,208 --> 00:17:41,041
You look like you could
collapse at any moment.

308
00:17:41,166 --> 00:17:42,166
Later.

309
00:17:42,208 --> 00:17:43,208
Please wait.

310
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,083
I simply cannot take this and offer nothing.

311
00:17:46,125 --> 00:17:50,000
Hati Skoll is just a sickeningly sweet guy.

312
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
He's also kind to boot.

313
00:17:52,041 --> 00:17:53,125
Especially to beautiful women.

314
00:17:53,166 --> 00:17:55,041
Y-You're lying!

315
00:17:55,083 --> 00:17:56,208
That's an awful accusation.

316
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,208
I'm sorry. It's just...

317
00:17:59,125 --> 00:18:02,000
My objective isn't that treasure.

318
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,083
It's a monster lurking below.

319
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:08,041
I thought only the floors leading up
to this chalice had been discovered...

320
00:18:08,083 --> 00:18:11,083
There's a monster that has
something I need right now.

321
00:18:11,083 --> 00:18:15,000
It just so happened that the call to conquer
the ruins coincided with my time here.

322
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,041
If that's why you're here,
this does make more sense, but...

323
00:18:18,083 --> 00:18:20,125
No, in that case, Sir Hati,

324
00:18:20,125 --> 00:18:24,083
would you please allow me
to at least guard you?

325
00:18:24,083 --> 00:18:25,083
What?

326
00:18:25,083 --> 00:18:29,000
All I can really offer right now
is my skill with this sword.

327
00:18:29,041 --> 00:18:31,166
I swear to you that I won't be a hindrance.

328
00:18:32,125 --> 00:18:33,166
Will you accept?

329
00:18:35,083 --> 00:18:37,041
M-My apologies.

330
00:18:37,125 --> 00:18:39,041
However, I cannot just accept
the Dragon Eye Chalice for free.

331
00:18:39,041 --> 00:18:40,166
- However, I cannot just accept
the Dragon Eye Chalice for free.
- No sign of her relenting.

332
00:18:40,208 --> 00:18:41,208
However, I cannot just accept
the Dragon Eye Chalice for free.

333
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,125
She must feel strongly
about repaying her debts.

334
00:18:44,125 --> 00:18:46,166
So what should I do?

335
00:18:47,166 --> 00:18:49,083
Can I add a few conditions?

336
00:18:49,166 --> 00:18:50,166
Yes.

337
00:18:51,041 --> 00:18:55,083
As a rule of thumb, we avoid questions prying
into each other's circumstances.

338
00:18:55,125 --> 00:18:58,208
We're just a bodyguard and client.

339
00:18:58,208 --> 00:19:00,083
Understood.

340
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:04,083
Also, I won't necessarily return
to the surface within the day.

341
00:19:04,125 --> 00:19:09,000
So if you want to return on your own,
I won't be responsible for you.

342
00:19:09,041 --> 00:19:11,000
If that's okay, it's nice working with you.

343
00:19:11,041 --> 00:19:12,166
Thank you very much.

344
00:19:12,166 --> 00:19:16,166
I shall protect you, Sir Hati,
even if it costs me my life.

345
00:19:30,125 --> 00:19:32,041
That was splendid work.

346
00:19:32,125 --> 00:19:33,208
Thank you.

347
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
What is it?

348
00:19:37,083 --> 00:19:40,000
Well, I wanted to ask you about something.

349
00:19:40,041 --> 00:19:42,083
About monsters with golden
eyes and those without.

350
00:19:42,083 --> 00:19:43,208
Oh, of course.

351
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,041
Monsters with golden eyes are said
to hold a great deal of "experience,"

352
00:19:47,041 --> 00:19:52,000
and they're recognized as the perfect prey
for heroes from another world to "level up."

353
00:19:52,166 --> 00:19:55,083
Are you familiar with the concept
of otherworld heroes?

354
00:19:55,083 --> 00:19:56,125
I am.

355
00:19:56,166 --> 00:20:00,166
Apparently they gain no experience
from killing other people.

356
00:20:00,166 --> 00:20:03,208
I hear experience points
are a feature unique to monsters.

357
00:20:04,125 --> 00:20:07,083
Explains why I got nothing from those guys.

358
00:20:08,041 --> 00:20:11,041
And how are monsters
without golden eyes regarded?

359
00:20:11,083 --> 00:20:13,000
They're regular monsters.

360
00:20:13,041 --> 00:20:16,000
Some are capable of forming
positive relationships with humans.

361
00:20:16,041 --> 00:20:17,000
I see.

362
00:20:17,041 --> 00:20:19,208
According to legend, the demon king,
who is the root of all evil,

363
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,041
radiates a special energy
known as demon king essence.

364
00:20:23,083 --> 00:20:26,083
Monsters strongly influenced
by it turn golden-eyed.

365
00:20:26,166 --> 00:20:31,000
It unleashes the instinct for violence
that all monsters harbor.

366
00:20:31,041 --> 00:20:32,166
Golden-eyed monsters...

367
00:20:32,166 --> 00:20:34,125
Gold... A golden hero...

368
00:20:34,208 --> 00:20:37,041
That golden hue is a sign.

369
00:20:37,125 --> 00:20:39,041
That's a little ominous.

370
00:20:47,041 --> 00:20:48,208
I sense the presence of a monster.

371
00:20:49,041 --> 00:20:50,000
A monster?

372
00:20:50,041 --> 00:20:54,166
It's not strong, so I paid it no mind,
but I keep sensing it.

373
00:20:54,208 --> 00:20:56,208
It's very close by.

374
00:20:57,083 --> 00:20:58,041
Piggymaru.

375
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:00,083
This is Piggymaru.

376
00:21:00,125 --> 00:21:02,166
Long story short, we're partners.

377
00:21:02,166 --> 00:21:04,083
I hope you two will get along.

378
00:21:04,125 --> 00:21:05,083
Go ahead.

379
00:21:05,125 --> 00:21:07,125
Are you sure it's safe?

380
00:21:11,166 --> 00:21:14,000
I'm Mist Balukas.

381
00:21:14,041 --> 00:21:15,166
It's a pleasure to meet you,

382
00:21:15,208 --> 00:21:17,000
Sir Piggymaru.

383
00:21:19,208 --> 00:21:22,041
It's a very cute slime.

384
00:21:22,041 --> 00:21:24,041
It's oddly comforting.

385
00:21:24,041 --> 00:21:25,166
Let's take a break here.

386
00:21:25,208 --> 00:21:27,041
You can get some light sleep.

387
00:21:27,041 --> 00:21:29,000
I'll wake you when it's time to leave.

388
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,208
No, I'm fine.

389
00:21:31,041 --> 00:21:33,125
Would you at least lie down for a while?

390
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:36,041
It won't do me any good if you
collapse partway through.

391
00:21:37,041 --> 00:21:38,083
Very well.

392
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:40,166
I'll at least lie down, then.

393
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Piggymaru.

394
00:21:48,166 --> 00:21:50,000
Sir Piggymaru?

395
00:21:50,041 --> 00:21:51,041
Sleep.

396
00:21:54,083 --> 00:21:57,083
There, now she should be
able to get some rest.

397
00:22:05,166 --> 00:22:07,125
I'd guessed as much.

398
00:22:08,041 --> 00:22:11,000
But you really are the former
knight captain of Holy Neah...

399
00:22:11,041 --> 00:22:13,000
Seras Ashrain, huh?

400
00:22:16,166 --> 00:22:21,083
Looks like their corpses were eaten by
monsters, but I guess this means it's true.

401
00:22:21,083 --> 00:22:24,125
Four Holy Watchers were killed here
in the blink of an eye

402
00:22:24,166 --> 00:22:27,083
without any real sign of battle.

403
00:22:27,083 --> 00:22:30,083
Who could do this to such skilled men?

404
00:22:30,166 --> 00:22:34,166
Seras Ashrain, with her Spirit Regalia.

405
00:22:34,208 --> 00:22:38,000
CIVIT GARTLAND
HUMANITY'S STRONGEST
- Will you provide me with some excitement?

406
00:24:10,166 --> 00:24:14,208
THE CHAIN KNOWN AS TRUST

